# === Session scratch / local-only working dirs (keep on disk, don't track) ===
# Unzipped marketplace pack source (the zip is the SSOT; this is an extract-on-demand working copy).
Tools/_laser_src/
# Skill BUNDLES dropped into Tools/skills as raw .skill ZIPs (the visual-spec source, e.g.
# expert-game-designer.skill). Installed skills live in Tools/skills/<name>/SKILL.md folders; the
# raw bundles are local references, not tracked.
Tools/skills/*.skill
# Temporary diagnostic content (B_*_AssignCharacterPart probes etc) — session scratch, never shipped.
Content/_TmpDiag/
# Agent scratch markers
Tools/_commit_msg*.txt
Tools/_commit_canary.txt
Tools/_gate2_live.png

# === EOS credentials — SECRET-SAFE (Track-2 EOS auth lane) ===
# The real Config/Custom/EOS/DefaultEngine.ini carries the operator's EOS ClientSecret +
# the 5 product IDs. UE's CustomConfig layering merges ONLY this named file (no #include,
# no arbitrary extra .ini), so the secret MUST live in this file — therefore the file is
# gitignored and only DefaultEngine.ini.example (placeholders, secret-free) is committed.
# Operator: copy the .example to DefaultEngine.ini, fill the 6 values, never commit.
Config/Custom/EOS/DefaultEngine.ini
!Config/Custom/EOS/DefaultEngine.ini.example

# === AFL hygiene (2026-06-23): marketplace demo dupes + parked vendor plugin ===
# Marketplace / anim-pack Demo/ subtrees are unreferenced demo dupes. gitignore never untracks, so
# nothing committed is affected -- this only keeps the dupes out of `git status`.
#
# ⚠ CORRECTED 2026-07-30. The original note claimed "the ignored remainder (SKM_Manny_Simple, demo
# materials/textures/maps) has no inbound refs." That was FALSE. A dependency sweep found FOUR tracked
# assets reaching into ignored Demo/ subtrees:
#     IK_AFL_VoxelPack + RTG_AFL_VoxelPack_to_Lyra   -> FreeAnimationLibrary/Demo/.../SKM_Manny_Simple
#     IK_AFL_EpicSample + RTG_AFL_EpicSample_to_Lyra -> FreeSampleAnimationSet/Demo/.../SKM_Manny
# i.e. tracked assets whose source skeleton is deliberately excluded -> they load with a NULL source on
# any fresh clone. All four had ZERO external referencers (their live output is the AFL_*_Retargeted
# AnimSequences, which do not depend on the marketplace source) and were DELETED, which is what makes
# the "no inbound refs" claim true rather than assumed. If a future retarget re-creates such an asset,
# it re-creates this clone break -- check with a tracked-refs-untracked-target sweep, do not assume.
**/Demo/

# --- Marketplace animation packs: IGNORED WHOLESALE (2026-07-30) ---------------------------------
# ~756 untracked files, ~849 MB, on a 250 GB LFS repo. Previously untracked-but-NOT-ignored, so a
# blind `git add .` would have committed every byte. Ignoring each pack ENTIRELY rather than only its
# Demo/ subtree: the half-ignored state above is precisely what produced the clone breaks.
#
# ⚠ Content/FreeAnimationLibrary is MIXED -- 18 files are already TRACKED (the climb animations +
# AM_AFL_ClimbWarp, load-bearing for the CLIMB system). Ignoring the directory does NOT untrack them;
# they stay committed, diffable and functional. The ignore only stops the 88 untracked siblings from
# appearing in status.
/Content/Fab/
/Content/FreeAnimationLibrary/
/Content/FreeSampleAnimationSet/
/Content/FreeLadderAnimationSet/
/Content/DynamicFalling/

# --- Source art that landed in Content/ instead of _Bridge (2026-07-30) --------------------------
# Raw .wav sources sitting beside their imported SoundWave .uasset. The imported assets ARE committed;
# these are the originals. ⚠ The directory name contains a SPACE, which is a cook/path hazard in
# Content/ -- if these are needed, relocate to Content/AFL/_Bridge/ with an underscore name.
/Content/Effects/Audio Sound Effects/
# Gib source FBX; source meshes belong under Content/AFL/_Bridge/, not Content/BagMan/.
/Content/BagMan/Characters/Dismember/SM_AFL_RobotHead_Gib.fbx
# OmniWalk vendor plugin: PARKED (kept on disk, not committed, not deleted) -- needed later for the
# gravity-gun lane. Untracked + ignored so it stops cluttering status without being lost.
/Plugins/OmniWalk07f218f7e14eV2/

